{
 "note": "Post hoc, 2026-10-19, extended 2026-10-20 (DEVIATIONS #15). No committed value is refit or changed. Records that share a player and an IL start date are records of one stint that the census kept because their transaction text differed (its duplicate rule matches the full text). Outcome labels are built from IL start dates (pitcher.py label_starts, batter.py cases), so a stint counts once in a label however many records it has, and it enters a label if any of its records qualifies: a family's label if any record is coded to that family, and the all-cause label unless every record is a COVID-era blank. Descriptive values include the repeated records. The A2 horizon output (the paper's Table S4) counts an IL start once for each of its records in the row's family (every record, for any IL), and the A2 anatomy output (Table S5) gives every record of a start the family of the start's first record. labels_if_first_record_only counts the panel rows whose label or removal flag would differ if only each stint's first record (by posting date, then transaction id) were kept, and stops_if_first_record_only the batter-seasons whose stop (the first musculoskeletal placement of the season, after which a batter's games are dropped) would move; the stop also takes any record. near_duplicates are stints of one player that start 1 to 3 days apart, with the same club and the same or a blank diagnosis, the later one starting before the earlier one ends: probably one stint posted twice, which the census counts as two; the alternative merges the later stint's records into the earlier stint. thumb_ucl: sites.py codes a thumb UCL injury as a UCL graft (elbow family); the alternative codes those records to the hand. median_il_days repeats the median IL stint of framing_f2.py (all seasons) and of the addendum A2 check (from 2015) from every record, as committed, and under both census alternatives.",
